{"id":"int-92cc00a7","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-06-09T20:04:56.831157626Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-908","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"send_alert_delivery now returns early (already_sent) if status==sent. Ticket channels (Jira/Linear) persist external issue id/key into payload_snapshot and skip creation if already present; the id is committed immediately after creation (before the final status=sent commit) so a SIGKILL in that window can't create a duplicate ticket on re-run. _post_json returns the parsed response; _send_jira_issue/_send_linear_issue return (id, key). Tests: idempotent resend (status guard) and skip-creation-when-id-present (crash-window guard)."}}
{"id":"int-aa5eca5c","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-06-09T20:04:59.211683111Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-tnh","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Added rate_limit_trust_forwarded_for setting (default False). _client_key now only honors X-Forwarded-For when the setting is enabled (trusted-proxy deployments); otherwise uses request.client.host, so rotating XFF can no longer spray fresh buckets. Spoofed-XFF test in test_security_middleware.py."}}
